HARN also: `eprintln(hide())` and `write_file(..., hide())` refuse.

## Honest holes (do not close SPRINT B6/B2 on "cheap")

PV1: cap names are a name-text override. A user `fn env_get(...) -> Int` can false-ERR / false-OK. `type Result = Int` can poison. Sibling checkers (`tc_ann_let`, `tc_call_eq`) still only see zero-arg calls. `return f(...);` still walks parens to find `;`.

MEM: B2 does not bound RSS. `try_scan_string` builds the whole string first. Import concat has no 64 KiB gate. `list_push` still copies. B8 leftover is real (~12 GB).

PV2 residuals (not a miss of the claim): 7-deep wrap chain, user `fn leak(s) { println(s); }`, `(hide)()`, non-String return, wasm/bc no check.

SEC: no new cap surface.

